# JSONPlaceholder
A server for practice:  someone's todos to tick, add and remove, and posts with their comments.
Every thing it shows is in JSONPlaceholder.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
It answers each change as if it saved it, and keeps nothing:  what you add here is gone when it's asked again.

<spell-thing "jsonplaceholder page">
	<spell>
		- its "new todo" is a new todo with user id = 1
	</spell>
	<property "person" description="Whose todos and posts these are:  the first person it has">the jsonplaceholder user whose id is 1</property>
	<property "todos" description="Theirs, from every todo">every todo where its user id is 1</property>

	<action "add the new todo">
		add its new todo to the saved todos
		set its new todo to a new todo with user id = 1
	</action>

	<draw>
		<header size="large">Practice, on JSONPlaceholder</header>
		<text color="grey">Tick a todo, add one, remove one:  each goes to the server, which answers as if it saved it, and keeps nothing.</text>
		<header size="medium">Their todos</header>
		draw its checklist
		<header size="medium">What they wrote</header>
		<for post in its person's posts loading="Asking JSONPlaceholder" failed="JSONPlaceholder can't be reached just now." />
		<text size="small">
			From <link link="https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com">JSONPlaceholder</link>, asked for as you look.
		</text>
	</draw>

	<draw "checklist">
		<form value={its new todo}>
			<field label="Something to do">
				<input name="title" placeholder="Water the plants" />
			</field>
		</form>
		<button size="small" color="primary" disabled={its new todo's title is ""} onClick={add the new todo}>Add</button>
		<for todo in its todos loading="Asking JSONPlaceholder" failed="JSONPlaceholder can't be reached just now." />
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# A todo
Ticked as it's done;  each tick, and each removal, goes to the server at once.

<spell-more-of "todo">
	<draw>
		<form value={it}>
			<stack direction="horizontal" align="center">
				<ui-checkbox name="completed" label={its title} />
				<button icon="close" size="mini" appearance="transparent" aria-label="Remove" title="Remove" onClick={remove it from the saved todos}/>
			</stack>
		</form>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# A post
Its title, what it says, and its comments:  read from the post's own address, the first time it's drawn.

<spell-more-of "post">
	<draw>
		<header size="small">{its title}</header>
		<text>{its body}</text>
		<for comment in its comments loading="Asking for its comments" />
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>

Each comment, as Spell UI draws one:  named in full, `<ui-comment>`, as `<comment>` is a comment in spellml.

<spell-more-of "comment">
	<draw>
		<ui-comment>
			<content>
				<author>{its email}</author>
				<description>{its body}</description>
			</content>
		</ui-comment>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>
